WEBVTT

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.147
while finalizing his historic work

00:03:30.147 --> 00:03:33.129
introducing the theory of Evolution.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:35.572
But the chicken’s greatest
contribution to science

00:03:35.572 --> 00:03:36.981
was yet to come.

00:03:36.981 --> 00:03:38.609
In the early 20th century,

00:03:38.609 --> 00:03:40.495
a trio of British scientists

00:03:40.495 --> 00:03:43.881
conducted extensive crossbreeding
of chickens,

00:03:43.881 --> 00:03:45.406
building on Gregor Mendel’s

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.928
studies of genetic inheritance.

00:03:47.928 --> 00:03:49.699
With their high genetic diversity,

00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:51.170
many distinct traits,

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.776
and only 7 months between generations,

00:03:53.776 --> 00:03:56.462
chickens were the perfect subject.

00:03:56.462 --> 00:03:59.378
This work resulted in the famous
Punnett Square,

00:03:59.378 --> 00:04:02.443
used to show the genotypes
that would result